WEBVTT

00:21.951 --> 00:25.541
I see. So, Canute is dead?

00:28.091 --> 00:32.091
No. He went missing, to be precise.

00:33.051 --> 00:36.431
Ragnar's unit tried to rescue Canute,

00:36.511 --> 00:39.311
and engaged Thorkell in battle at Marlborough.

00:40.351 --> 00:41.971
In the midst of the confusion,

00:42.061 --> 00:44.691
His Highness the Prince went missing.

00:48.111 --> 00:52.571
Then aren't they still surrounded by Thorkell's men?

00:52.651 --> 00:56.781
Yes. However, we didn't see anyone among
Thorkell's men

00:56.861 --> 01:01.491
who looked like he could be the prince for two days.

01:03.371 --> 01:07.001
He may still be alive and is waiting for help.

01:08.081 --> 01:10.591
However, even if we were to send help,

01:10.671 --> 01:13.591
we'd have to wait until spring.

01:13.671 --> 01:16.131
I'm sure you must be very worried,

01:16.221 --> 01:18.511
Your Highness.

01:22.681 --> 01:24.851
If Canute

01:24.931 --> 01:27.481
had been as talented

01:27.561 --> 01:29.771
as his brother Harald,

01:31.151 --> 01:36.241
he might not have
ended up missing.

03:13.751 --> 03:15.171
Wow! It's snowing!

03:15.251 --> 03:16.251
AFTER YULE

03:16.341 --> 03:19.511
The war is ending!

03:19.591 --> 03:20.721
Winter.

03:20.801 --> 03:22.591
DECEMBER 1013
GLOUCESTER, EARLDOM OF MERCIA

03:22.681 --> 03:26.141
You're cold enough to freeze even a warrior's heart.

03:26.221 --> 03:28.891
Oh, winter!

03:28.971 --> 03:32.521
Captain. Roasted pork or boiled pork.
What do you want?

03:32.601 --> 03:33.601
Give me both!

03:39.821 --> 03:42.571
I can't understand you. Swallow your food first.

03:42.661 --> 03:43.661
Okay.

03:45.821 --> 03:48.491
In any case,

03:48.581 --> 03:51.911
the fact that the prince escaped was a big loss to us.

03:52.001 --> 03:54.751
He didn't escape! You handed him over.

03:54.831 --> 03:59.921
That prince was a coward,
but he could have been useful.

04:00.011 --> 04:03.471
We could have put him on a pedestal
and started a new dynasty.

04:03.551 --> 04:06.391
It would have helped gather soldiers for an army
at least.

04:06.471 --> 04:09.181
If you're the one who's going to carry him,

04:09.261 --> 04:11.431
you'd be pretty powerful.

04:11.521 --> 04:13.601
Indeed. What?

04:13.691 --> 04:16.271
Hey, you! English girl!

04:16.361 --> 04:17.651
Yes?

04:17.731 --> 04:20.111
Beer! Bring a keg!

04:20.191 --> 04:23.201
Excuse me! They ordered another keg!

04:23.281 --> 04:25.741
Another one? Damn!

04:25.821 --> 04:29.951
Those rascals! They're going to eat through
the entire city!

04:30.041 --> 04:33.001
This is robbery!

04:33.081 --> 04:34.671
Stop crying!

04:38.501 --> 04:43.421
If I was going to lose the prince anyway,
I should have given him to the English instead.

04:45.431 --> 04:46.891
What?

04:46.971 --> 04:49.511
You're so difficult.

04:49.601 --> 04:53.481
As soon as the fire starts to die down,
you go looking for another spark.

04:53.561 --> 04:56.061
Of course, you bastard!

04:56.151 --> 04:58.861
We're warriors!

04:58.941 --> 05:01.611
A warrior is a warrior when he's on the battlefield!

05:04.781 --> 05:05.781
But you know...

05:05.901 --> 05:08.741
I heard some bad news about that.

05:10.241 --> 05:13.041
They're going to recognize King Sweyn
as the Bretwalda

05:13.121 --> 05:16.871
at the next Witenagemot in Wessex.

05:16.961 --> 05:18.251
What?

05:18.331 --> 05:20.671
That's total surrender!

05:20.751 --> 05:24.381
That's right. Denmark is going
to swallow England whole.

05:24.471 --> 05:28.221
The nobility want to end the war, even if it means
surrendering the throne.

05:30.471 --> 05:33.971
Every time I get a bad feeling about something,
why does it always come true?

05:34.061 --> 05:38.191
What are you going to do? Attack King Sweyn,
even if it means certain death?

05:38.271 --> 05:39.521
You idiot!

05:39.611 --> 05:43.571
I love fighting, but I hate losing!

05:43.651 --> 05:45.441
When I fight, I fight to win!

05:51.371 --> 05:53.241
This is no fun.

05:53.331 --> 05:57.711
I wish the world would be at war forever.

05:59.041 --> 06:01.541
It's a messenger! Is the lord here?

06:07.671 --> 06:09.591
Anything out of the ordinary, Ear?

06:09.681 --> 06:11.801
There sure is. It's damn cold.

06:13.101 --> 06:14.311
The snow absorbs sounds.

06:14.391 --> 06:17.351
NORTH PART OF EARLDOM OF MERCIA
ASKELADD'S ARMY CONTROLLED FARM VILLAGE

06:17.431 --> 06:18.941
Even I can't hear that far anymore.

06:19.021 --> 06:21.941
It's better than keeping guards all over the place.

06:22.021 --> 06:24.191
We can avoid giving away our position.

06:25.361 --> 06:28.991
Then do something about those guys.

06:29.071 --> 06:31.871
They're obviously not farmers.

06:31.951 --> 06:36.581
-Monks? Keep an eye on them, too.
-Father, forgive us.

06:36.661 --> 06:40.211
"Forgive us." Hear that?

06:40.291 --> 06:44.671
Must they constantly beg for forgiveness?

06:44.751 --> 06:46.001
What a pain.

06:48.761 --> 06:51.091
Oh, God Most High,

06:51.181 --> 06:53.851
Our Father in Heaven,

06:53.931 --> 06:56.891
please gather the souls of the villagers

06:56.971 --> 06:59.941
who lie in rest here to your side.

07:00.021 --> 07:04.441
Please save the souls of the men who killed
these people.

07:04.521 --> 07:07.481
Please forgive us for our sins.

07:10.951 --> 07:14.321
This isn't the time to be praying for someone else,
you bastards.

07:21.211 --> 07:22.791
Father.

07:22.881 --> 07:26.341
Can you hear my voice?

07:29.091 --> 07:30.631
Our Father.

07:31.431 --> 07:32.841
You

07:32.931 --> 07:36.261
created us in your image.

07:37.351 --> 07:40.351
But you didn't give us your power.

07:42.271 --> 07:43.311
Father.

07:44.521 --> 07:48.361
If you love both good men and bad men equally,

07:49.481 --> 07:53.281
why do you test us, despite our powerlessness?

07:54.621 --> 07:55.621
Father.

07:56.871 --> 07:58.701
Can you

07:58.791 --> 08:01.211
hear my voice?

08:02.501 --> 08:03.791
Our Father.

08:05.251 --> 08:07.041
I doubt

08:08.421 --> 08:10.301
-your love.
-Enough!

08:20.471 --> 08:22.351
Did you say...

08:22.431 --> 08:23.851
you doubt the Father?

08:28.941 --> 08:33.201
And you call yourself a Christian?
You should fear the Lord!

08:33.281 --> 08:36.201
We must not doubt the Father's love!

08:40.161 --> 08:41.161
Every father...

08:42.541 --> 08:46.581
Every father loves his own child.

08:50.841 --> 08:51.841
Your Highness...

08:54.881 --> 08:56.511
Oh! Wait!

09:07.151 --> 09:08.311
Father...

09:11.231 --> 09:12.821
An army of Danes?

09:12.901 --> 09:14.321
Really?

09:14.401 --> 09:16.951
Yes. That's what the message said.

09:17.031 --> 09:21.451
They've occupied a village
at the head of the Severn River.

09:21.541 --> 09:24.911
We've received a request for reinforcements
from the local lord.

09:25.001 --> 09:28.041
According to one of the villagers who survived,

09:28.131 --> 09:30.921
the enemy has around 100 to 200 men.

09:31.001 --> 09:35.591
Soldiers from neighboring areas are already
heading there,

09:35.671 --> 09:39.431
but we wanted to ask you to come too, Thorkell,
because of your military fame.

09:39.511 --> 09:42.931
-What do you think?
-Nothing, really.

09:43.021 --> 09:47.021
There aren't a lot of Danish units who would
act alone there

09:47.101 --> 09:49.401
at this time of year.

09:49.481 --> 09:52.861
They feigned to go by sea,
but they're heading to Gainsborough by land.

09:53.861 --> 09:57.611
They must have been snowed in and are stuck.

09:57.701 --> 09:59.571
I'm almost certain it's...

10:03.451 --> 10:06.501
Thorfinn and Canute.

10:06.581 --> 10:10.381
All right! Wake everyone up! Get ready to march!

10:11.381 --> 10:12.631
And...

10:12.711 --> 10:14.631
Hey, you.

10:14.711 --> 10:17.471
Pack us some lunch.

10:17.551 --> 10:20.641
For 500 men. Five days will be enough.

10:20.721 --> 10:23.141
Five hundred?

10:25.101 --> 10:27.481
Here we go.

10:27.561 --> 10:31.771
This is fun. If we do this right,

10:32.941 --> 10:35.981
we can enjoy this war for a long time!

10:46.161 --> 10:48.331
How many men are there? Ear?

10:48.411 --> 10:51.331
Who knows? Maybe 50, or 100.

10:51.421 --> 10:55.301
They're extending their line to the east along the forest.

10:55.381 --> 10:58.131
They discovered us quickly.

10:58.221 --> 10:59.631
Did we make a mistake somewhere?

10:59.721 --> 11:01.801
I don't know...

11:01.891 --> 11:04.641
They found us. We can't change that.

11:04.721 --> 11:06.641
We're leaving?

11:06.721 --> 11:08.981
Tonight? That's impossible!

11:09.061 --> 11:11.481
I've only finished two sleds!

11:11.561 --> 11:13.561
I just started on the third one yesterday!

11:13.651 --> 11:17.731
Really? Thanks. Then finish them by tonight.

11:17.821 --> 11:19.901
We'll abandon the ones we can't finish.

11:19.991 --> 11:21.991
I said that's impossible!

11:22.071 --> 11:24.121
We only have two carpenters!

11:24.201 --> 11:26.991
The English army found us.

11:27.081 --> 11:29.161
-They found us?
-Yeah.

11:29.251 --> 11:31.921
They came through the snow.

11:32.001 --> 11:34.171
They must really hate the Danes.

11:34.251 --> 11:35.291
Impossible...

11:35.381 --> 11:37.881
We must hurry, or we'll miss our chance
to escape.

11:39.211 --> 11:40.841
Understand? Hurry and finish.

11:40.921 --> 11:42.721
Okay.

11:42.801 --> 11:45.801
Bjorn! Prepare the men for battle.

11:45.891 --> 11:49.771
Capture their commander.
I want to find out how they found us.

11:49.851 --> 11:51.561
Understood.

11:51.641 --> 11:53.651
Wait, Bjorn.

11:53.731 --> 11:55.771
One more thing.

11:55.861 --> 11:57.151
This is a good opportunity.

11:57.231 --> 11:59.571
Let's do what we discussed as well.

12:01.741 --> 12:02.781
They found us?

12:03.861 --> 12:05.911
This is bad.

12:05.991 --> 12:09.911
We'll be fine! The English are weak.

12:10.001 --> 12:12.371
No. That's not what I mean.

12:12.461 --> 12:14.671
I was talking about Askeladd's luck.

12:14.751 --> 12:16.251
Luck?

12:16.331 --> 12:18.671
First the heavy snowfall, and now this.

12:18.751 --> 12:22.801
This is the first time his plans have ever been ruined.

12:29.641 --> 12:32.981
Oh! What a tasty-looking rabbit!

12:33.061 --> 12:37.311
-Are you the one who caught it, Thorfinn?
-What?

12:37.401 --> 12:40.861
Are you going to eat it alone? Are you going to roast it?

12:40.941 --> 12:43.281
Why do you care?

12:43.361 --> 12:45.241
It's not good to eat nothing but meat!

12:45.321 --> 12:47.991
Boil it with some vegetables!

12:48.071 --> 12:50.621
I'll make some soup with that rabbit.

12:51.911 --> 12:56.001
Shut up. I can eat my own food however I want.

12:56.081 --> 12:59.381
You're going to borrow someone's stove anyway, right?

12:59.461 --> 13:00.631
Come over here!

13:04.421 --> 13:07.511
Your Highness! I've brought broad beans,
cabbage, and rabbit!

13:07.591 --> 13:08.601
Rabbit?

13:08.681 --> 13:11.311
Yes. Thorfinn caught it.

13:11.391 --> 13:13.731
I thought it would be good to add to the soup.

13:20.151 --> 13:21.321
Thanks.

13:21.401 --> 13:23.151
Drain the blood and remove its organs.

13:34.541 --> 13:37.541
The ingredients are simple, but it tastes good.

13:37.621 --> 13:38.881
It's because of the rabbit.

13:38.961 --> 13:42.421
I've grown tired of eating salted-cured meat. Thank you.

13:45.801 --> 13:47.551
What's wrong? Don't hold back.

13:47.631 --> 13:49.051
It's your rabbit.

13:56.351 --> 13:59.941
It's good, right? Catch us a deer next time!

14:02.191 --> 14:05.191
I thought royals only did the eating.

14:05.281 --> 14:08.361
It's my hobby. I don't usually cook.

14:08.451 --> 14:10.911
No one knows about it except Ragnar.

14:10.991 --> 14:13.541
You can't tell anyone either, okay?

14:13.621 --> 14:15.451
There's nothing wrong with it.

14:17.081 --> 14:18.751
A long time ago,

14:18.831 --> 14:20.671
I cooked some cod.

14:21.751 --> 14:23.501
It turned out well,

14:23.591 --> 14:25.761
so I brought it to my father.

14:33.561 --> 14:36.521
But His Highness didn't eat it.

14:36.601 --> 14:38.941
He was very angry.

14:39.021 --> 14:42.811
"You're the child of a king! Don't act like a slave!"
That's what he said.

14:43.981 --> 14:47.241
I wasn't supposed to cook after that.

14:48.451 --> 14:51.071
A king's child doesn't need to know how to do
things like this.

14:55.791 --> 14:57.251
At that time,

14:57.331 --> 15:00.581
His Highness must have been very busy.

15:00.671 --> 15:04.541
When this war is over, let's cook some poultry
and bring it to him.

15:04.631 --> 15:06.761
I'm sure he'd be happy.

15:11.011 --> 15:12.801
What kind of poultry?

15:12.891 --> 15:15.101
I've never cooked poultry before.

15:15.181 --> 15:17.561
Chicken, or duck.

15:17.641 --> 15:21.311
Do you remember the duck you ate during Yule?

15:21.391 --> 15:23.481
Yes. That was delicious.

15:23.561 --> 15:26.481
I asked the cook for his secret.

15:26.571 --> 15:29.191
He made good use of the broth.

15:29.281 --> 15:31.451
The broth? I see.

15:33.411 --> 15:35.331
Ragnar!

15:35.411 --> 15:37.581
You idiot! I have a message!

15:39.371 --> 15:41.371
What is it? What's wrong?

15:41.461 --> 15:43.671
The enemy has found us.

15:43.751 --> 15:46.291
A battle has begun in the woods to the east.

15:46.381 --> 15:47.551
What?

15:48.511 --> 15:50.511
They don't have a lot of men,

15:50.591 --> 15:52.431
but please be careful.

15:55.351 --> 15:56.721
What's going on?

15:56.811 --> 15:59.101
We've only been in this village for ten days!

15:59.181 --> 16:02.191
-How come they found us?
-How am I supposed to know?

16:05.151 --> 16:07.191
What's going on?

16:07.271 --> 16:10.191
We even killed all the villagers...

16:12.861 --> 16:14.451
In any case,

16:14.531 --> 16:17.701
we're going to move once we defeat the English.
Get ready.

16:17.781 --> 16:19.161
That's why I first said

16:19.241 --> 16:21.621
we should turn back to Wales!

16:21.711 --> 16:23.711
No. We're heading for Derby.

16:25.381 --> 16:27.091
He still wants to keep walking through

16:27.171 --> 16:29.341
enemy lands in this situation?

16:29.421 --> 16:32.671
Bring Askeladd here. Now!

16:32.761 --> 16:35.681
He's leading at the frontline right now.

16:35.761 --> 16:38.971
If you want to talk to him, you should go
see him yourself.

16:39.061 --> 16:40.221
I'll show you the way.

16:43.441 --> 16:46.861
Unbelievable! You men are just like your leader!

16:46.941 --> 16:48.611
You don't have any manners!

16:48.691 --> 16:51.781
He can't even read his own luck!

16:51.861 --> 16:53.491
And he's a Norse warrior?

16:53.571 --> 16:56.871
I swear on my sword, I'm going to show him

16:56.951 --> 16:58.491
how foolish he is today!

17:02.451 --> 17:03.581
Hey!

17:03.661 --> 17:05.121
Hey!

17:05.211 --> 17:07.381
The sound of the battle is coming from that way!

17:10.801 --> 17:13.971
You finally noticed? You're so slow.

17:14.051 --> 17:16.591
What? You bastards! What are you--?

17:37.951 --> 17:39.951
You bastards...

17:40.031 --> 17:42.701
Sorry, Conehead.

17:42.791 --> 17:44.831
It's orders from Askeladd.

17:55.921 --> 17:59.221
Want to fight? We're okay with that.

17:59.301 --> 18:01.431
But you're going to die anyway.

18:08.061 --> 18:12.441
Bring Askeladd here! I have something important
to tell him.

18:12.521 --> 18:15.861
Is it your dying wish? I'll listen. Tell me.

18:15.941 --> 18:18.151
Just bring him here!

18:18.241 --> 18:20.781
It's related to His Highness the Prince.

18:20.871 --> 18:22.241
I need to talk to him directly.

18:24.951 --> 18:26.081
Hurry!

18:27.121 --> 18:29.871
Let's hear your dying wish.

18:39.181 --> 18:41.261
Shall we speak in private?

18:44.261 --> 18:46.221
The cries stopped.

18:46.311 --> 18:47.851
The battle is over.

18:53.861 --> 18:54.861
Unbelievable.

18:56.031 --> 18:58.441
The soup got cold.

19:01.111 --> 19:04.281
I'm grateful to you.

19:04.371 --> 19:08.751
You did a good job keeping that coward of a prince alive.

19:08.831 --> 19:10.831
Your death will cause him to grow

19:10.921 --> 19:13.251
even further.

19:14.631 --> 19:18.551
I will take over that job starting today,

19:18.631 --> 19:20.631
in place of you, who was

19:21.801 --> 19:23.681
"killed by the English."

19:26.681 --> 19:29.141
Swear to your god!

19:29.231 --> 19:32.441
Swear that you'll take over for me,

19:32.521 --> 19:33.901
and that...

19:35.731 --> 19:38.901
you'll protect His Highness Canute
at whatever the cost!

19:42.531 --> 19:46.031
I will protect His Highness Canute
at whatever the cost,

19:46.121 --> 19:49.661
and ensure that Ragnar the warrior
did not die in vain.

19:50.871 --> 19:51.961
Are you satisfied?

19:53.171 --> 19:55.211
It fills me with regret

19:55.291 --> 19:58.671
to leave His Highness with you.

19:58.761 --> 20:00.671
You should hurry.

20:00.761 --> 20:04.051
You've lost a lot of blood.

20:09.811 --> 20:11.601
Before you reach

20:12.941 --> 20:14.271
Gainsborough,

20:15.481 --> 20:18.481
you should prepare yourself...

20:21.401 --> 20:23.991
The court in Jelling

20:24.071 --> 20:27.081
are fighting over who will be the next king of Denmark

20:27.161 --> 20:29.991
and has split into two factions.

20:31.161 --> 20:33.831
One of the factions picked His Highness Canute

20:33.921 --> 20:35.831
as their leader.

20:36.881 --> 20:40.091
The other faction chose Canute's brother,

20:40.171 --> 20:41.711
Harald.

20:42.801 --> 20:44.931
They don't care about what

20:45.011 --> 20:47.681
either of them wants.

20:47.761 --> 20:49.261
It's just a power struggle

20:49.351 --> 20:51.601
amongst those traitors.

20:53.021 --> 20:55.021
His Highness the King feared

20:55.101 --> 20:58.611
that the Kingdom of Denmark would be split.

21:00.021 --> 21:04.241
His heart was probably already decided.

21:09.621 --> 21:11.741
He decided to kill

21:11.831 --> 21:14.121
one of the princes.

21:14.211 --> 21:16.671
King Sweyn decided to kill the prince?

21:17.711 --> 21:19.671
The reason that the king

21:19.751 --> 21:22.551
took the prince to the battlefield with him

21:22.631 --> 21:25.471
was to have the prince die in battle.

21:26.681 --> 21:28.641
Be careful.

21:28.721 --> 21:31.641
Prince Canute's real enemy

21:32.561 --> 21:33.641
is now

21:34.561 --> 21:37.101
his father, King Sweyn

21:37.191 --> 21:39.061
himself.

21:40.821 --> 21:43.071
Go into exile.

21:43.151 --> 21:45.151
That's the only way now.

21:47.821 --> 21:49.911
In Gainsborough,

21:49.991 --> 21:53.371
my brother will make preparations

21:54.541 --> 21:56.541
for you...

22:05.091 --> 22:07.761
What's going on?

22:07.841 --> 22:10.761
You should have told me earlier.

22:13.181 --> 22:15.101
Please.

22:15.181 --> 22:16.431
Just one...

22:18.021 --> 22:19.231
last look...

22:20.231 --> 22:21.691
Let me see His Highness.

22:23.521 --> 22:25.191
To say goodbye...

22:26.901 --> 22:27.951
No.

22:33.371 --> 22:34.541
Your Highness...

22:35.541 --> 22:37.371
Once this war is over...

22:43.711 --> 22:46.301
let's cook poultry together.

22:47.471 --> 22:48.631
I'm sure

22:50.051 --> 22:53.431
the king would be...

22:55.771 --> 22:56.851
happy.
